# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — sex-stratified RA biomarker pipeline
#
# WHAT IS TRACKED: all code, all documentation, all results TABLES and FIGURES.
# A reader can therefore see every reported number and every figure, and can tie
# each one to the exact script version that produced it.
#
# WHAT IS NOT TRACKED: large binary intermediates and raw expression matrices.
# These are regenerable from the scripts, and several exceed GitHub's file-size
# limits. The cached network-derived artefacts (MR instruments, coloc regions)
# are the exception that matters for reproducibility — see REPRODUCIBILITY.md
# section 3 — and they must be archived alongside a release rather than in git.
# =============================================================================

# ---- raw data (symlink to a sibling tree; not self-contained) ----------------
data/raw/

# ---- large binary intermediates (regenerable) --------------------------------
*.rds
*.RData
*.rda
*.csv.gz

# ---- raw expression matrices at the repository root (15-34 MB each) ----------
GSE73622_expression_matrix.csv
GSE73622_Exprs_annotated.csv
GSE73622_probe_annotation.csv
GSE73622_sample_metadata.csv

# ---- oversized derived tables ------------------------------------------------
# Per-gene full DE tables and instrument tables run to tens of MB. The
# significant/summary versions ARE tracked.
results/tables/*_full.csv
results/tables/MR_*_TABLE1_instruments.csv
results/tables/DEG_interaction_full.csv
results/tables/DEG_celladjusted_*.csv

# ---- run artefacts -----------------------------------------------------------
results/logs/*.pid
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
renv/library/
renv/staging/

# ---- OS / editor -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*~
.Rproj.user

# ---- Python bytecode -----------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- Markdown docs (kept local, not pushed) -------------------------------
*.md
